// Akkado stdlib — scale quantization (auto-generated).
//
// AUTO-GENERATED FILE — DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.
//
// Generated from web/scripts/generate-scale-quantize.ts. To regenerate:
//     cd web && bun run scripts/generate-scale-quantize.ts
//
// Implements docs/prd-scale-quantize.md §4.4 (`scale`, degree mapping)
// and §4.5 (`key`, 12-TET quantization). Both are the outer `match`
// themselves — the literal-only constraint of match dispatchers (see
// scales.ak header) precludes delegating to `scale_intervals(name)`
// at runtime, so each branch inlines its own literal interval array.
//
// Catalog: 12 chromatic roots × 8 scale types.
// `key` strings are octave-agnostic (root only); `scale` strings carry
// the octave digit (e.g. `"d3:minor"`), with a missing digit defaulting
// to octave 3 per PRD §4.3.

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Closure-body math (inlined per branch)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// The key/scale closures inline `floor(note + 0.5)` (round-half-up) and
// `fmod(fmod(note, 12) + 12, 12)` (mod-12 that handles negative inputs)
// directly, rather than calling user-fn helpers. Reason: user-fn calls
// that materialize more than once in a closure body lower to BLOCK_CALL,
// and `run_event_map_closure` in the VM does not currently dispatch
// BLOCK_CALL from within a subprogram body (it would silently no-op).
// The inlined form uses only builtins (`floor`, `fmod`, `+`, `*`,
// `ARRAY_INDEX`), all of which `execute()` handles correctly.
//
// This duplicates the `floor(note + 0.5)` subexpression a few times per
// branch — the akkado codegen doesn't CSE buffers, so the cost is a
// handful of extra arithmetic instructions per event. Negligible at
// audio rates.

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// fn key — octave-agnostic 12-TET quantization. Per-scale delta tables
// computed at generation time (see web/scripts/generate-scale-quantize.ts
// `keyDeltaTable`).
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

